      "section": "conversion.faq-legacy",
      "content": {
        "theme": "olive-items",
        "eyebrow": "FAQ's",
        "title": "Every answer, right here",
        "items": [
          {
            "q": "How long does it take to launch Nimbus content?",
            "a": "The learning team began with a simple question about what people actually needed from their working day and how short, practical resources could fit around."
          },
          {
            "q": "How many learning resources do my teams receive?",
            "a": "Fit around busy shifts without adding pressure. Managers were invited to share the moments where support mattered most, and those conversations shaped a clear plan for the first year. Every new programme."
          },
          {
            "q": "Which content formats does the library include?",
            "a": "Clear plan for the first year. Every new programme launched with a small pilot group, so the team could listen closely, adjust the format and build confidence before rolling it out across every region. People responded well to bite-sized videos."
          },
          {
            "q": "Which languages does Nimbus content cover?",
            "a": "Format and build confidence before rolling it out across every region. People responded well to bite-sized videos, quick reads and guided activities that felt relevant to their own roles, and completion rates rose steadily as a result. Leaders noticed the change in team meetings, where colleagues."
          },
          {
            "q": "What makes Nimbus content different from other learning libraries?",
            "a": "Felt relevant to their own roles, and completion rates rose steadily as a result. Leaders noticed the change in team meetings, where colleagues started sharing tips and recommending."
          },
          {
            "q": "Why use LMS content?",
            "a": "Started sharing tips and recommending resources to each other without being asked. Clear dashboards made it easy to see which topics landed and where to focus next, so the plan stayed flexible and grounded in real feedback from."
          },
          {
            "q": "Who makes the best content for an LMS?",
            "a": "Where to focus next, so the plan stayed flexible and grounded in real feedback from the people using it every week. Over time the platform became the natural home for onboarding, product updates and everyday questions, replacing scattered documents and long email chains with."
          }
        ]
      },
